<Layout
	title="About"
	description="What is Stelth Robotics?"
	heroImage="/workshop.jpg"
>
	<h2>Background</h2>
	<p>
		Stelth Robotics was founded in 2026 with the mission to make robotic arms that are accessible to and desired
		by everyone. It's initial product, the Alpha-Mini, is a compact, affordable, and easy-to-use robotic
		arm designed for hobbyists, educators, and professionals alike. In 2027, Stelth will be releasing
		Alpha, the big brother of the Alpha-Mini, designed for a wide range of consumer facing and manufacturing
		applications. Stelth is led by <a href={`https://matthewfurkert.com`}>Matthew Furkert</a>, and in
		headquartered in Waterloo, Ontario. 
	</p>
	<h2>Careers</h2>
	<p>
		Stelth Robotics is looking for engineers who have a proven track record of exceptional work.
		If you are passionate about robotics and want to be part of a early stage company with unlimited
		growth potential, email evidence of your ability to careers@<i>domain_name</i>.
	</p>

</Layout>
